4258: \begin{theorem}[Exact-inclusion support-surface realization]
4259: \label{thm:exact-inclusion-support-surface-realization}
4260: For the current package the selected support branch is exact supplemental inclusion of \path{review_bundle/}, but this branch remains conditional until an external upload-or-archive instantiation record exists.  If the completed submission contains that directory with the certificate-file digests listed in
4261: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}, then every bundle-backed claim in
4262: this supplement has a submitted finite support surface at its stated
4263: path-verified evidence level.  If the exact directory is not submitted, then the
4264: same support conclusion holds only after replacing it by an archive satisfying
4265: the five tests of Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}; no venue upload receipt, public DOI, or archive locator is claimed for the present package.
4266: \end{theorem}
4267: 
4268: \begin{proof}
4269: The exact-inclusion hypothesis supplies the directory named in every bundle-local
4270: path and the final digest manifest named in
4271: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness}.  By that proposition,
4272: the manifest traverses the finite certificate surfaces used by the supplement:
4273: the bundle manifest, schema, current pass-record ledger, source-interface map,
4274: primary-claim inventory, verifier scripts, verifier logs, source snapshot, and
4275: case snapshots.  Matching the listed SHA-256 digests fixes the bytes of each of
4276: those certificate files at final packaging time, while preserving the relative
4277: path names by which the manuscript refers to them.  Thus every bundle-backed
4278: claim has the submitted finite evidence surface asserted for it, and the evidence
4279: level remains path-verified because the argument checks file presence and digest
4280: identity rather than rerunning Lean, daemons, or external artifacts.
4281: 
4282: If the exact directory is absent, the proof of
4283: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} shows that the only
4284: finite replacement accepted by this paper is an archive with the same manifest
4285: identity, bundle-version tuple, finite certificate file list, per-file SHA-256
4286: digests, and relative path semantics.  Those are exactly the five tests in
4287: Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}.  Without such an archive, at
4288: least one bundle-local path or digest row has no submitted representative, so the
4289: corresponding bundle-backed claim lacks its evidence surface.  The statement that
4290: no public DOI or archive locator is claimed is the support-mode selection in
4291: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness}; it records that this
4292: package takes the first admissible case, not the archive-equivalent case.
4293: \end{proof}
4294: 
4295: \begin{theorem}[Final support-surface closure]
4296: \label{thm:final-support-surface-closure}
4297: For the current package, using
4298: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention},
4299: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness}, and
4300: Theorem~\ref{thm:exact-inclusion-support-surface-realization}, the bundle-backed
4301: claims in this supplement are admissible at the stated path-verified evidence
4302: level exactly when the submitted supplemental material contains the exact
4303: directory \path{review_bundle/} whose final packaging record is
4304: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}.  The exact directory branch also
4305: requires that any post-generation change to a named bundle file be followed by
4306: refreshed SHA-256 rows in that final digest record and by rerunning the finite
4307: verifiers whose records cite the changed coordinate.  A replacement archive is not a
4308: current package branch; it would have to satisfy
4309: Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} and provide a locator before a
4310: future package could select it.  If the exact directory is not present in the
4311: current package submission, the bundle-backed claims are not part of the accepted
4312: support surface, although the short presentation artifact may still cite the
4313: pinned public \path{newmath} repository for the imported source spine.
4314: \end{theorem}
4315: 
4316: \begin{proof}
4317: Let $B$ denote the set of bundle-dependent claims in this supplement.  By the
4318: definition of \path{review_bundle/} in the problem statement and by the bundle
4319: rows of Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}, every claim in $B$
4320: uses at least one named certificate surface under \path{review_bundle/}: the
4321: manifest, certificate schema, pass-record ledger, source-interface map,
4322: primary-claim inventory, verifier scripts or logs, the pinned source snapshot,
4323: or one of the case snapshots.  Therefore a submitted support surface for $B$
4324: must either contain those named files with their relative path semantics or
4325: replace them by an archive that is finite-file-list and hash equivalent.
4326: 
4327: If the exact directory \path{review_bundle/} is uploaded, then
4328: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness} identifies it as the
4329: current concrete support witness and all named bundle paths are present in the submitted supplemental boundary.  The file
4330: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} records the final SHA-256 digest
4331: surface for those certificate files, so the byte identity of the supplied
4332: directory is checkable without changing the role of the directory into an
4333: archive claim.  If a named bundle file is regenerated after that digest surface
4334: is written, the byte-coordinate selected by the support relation changes; by
4335: Proposition~\ref{prop:regenerated-theorem-inventory-digest-closure} and the same
4336: finite-coordinate argument, the corresponding digest row and verifier logs must
4337: be refreshed before the regenerated file can be the submitted support witness.
4338: Hence all claims in $B$ have the path-verified support surface asserted for this
4339: package exactly in the exact-upload-with-current-digests branch.
4340: 
4341: The archive criterion remains a finite non-current rejection test.  If a later
4342: package attempted to replace the directory by an archive, Audit
4343: record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} would require equality of
4344: the manifest identity, bundle-version tuple, finite certificate file list,
4345: per-file SHA-256 digests, and relative path semantics.  The current package does
4346: not contain the locator or archive digest table needed to enter that branch, so
4347: the theorem cannot treat an archive as an accepted present support surface.
4348: 
4349: Conversely, suppose the exact directory is not submitted for the current package.
4350: Then at least one named bundle certificate surface is outside the submitted
4351: artifact boundary and has no selected finite replacement.  The finite certificate
4352: schema used in Theorem~\ref{thm:current-package-certificate-exactness}
4353: accepts only submitted paths, explicit historical path records, and the stated
4354: supplemental surfaces.  Hence the missing bundle surface cannot support the
4355: corresponding claim in $B$.  The public \path{newmath} repository citation is a
4356: separate pinned-source citation, so it remains available for the short
4357: architectural note but does not reconstitute the omitted bundle-backed
4358: certificate records.  This proves both admissible cases and the failure of all
4359: other cases.
4360: \end{proof}
