4413: \begin{theorem}[Workspace-to-final-package reconciliation]
4414: \label{thm:workspace-final-package-reconciliation}
4415: Let $H_0$ be the automath commit
4416: \path{305ee93353b16babc461bfad1a7aee9c808ee268}, and let $D_0$ be the digest
4417: manifest \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}.  The source-state claim
4418: made in Audit record~\ref{prop:final-immutable-package-state-certificate} is the
4419: finite package claim $(H_0,D_0)$, not a claim that every later reviewer checkout,
4420: editor workspace, or post-packaging working tree has Git \path{HEAD} equal to $H_0$.  If a
4421: current workspace reports a different Git \path{HEAD}, then the verifier-log and
4422: bundle-backed claims of this supplement remain admissible exactly in the
4423: following two reconciled cases:
4424: \begin{enumerate}
4425: \item the submitted support surface is exact inclusion of \path{review_bundle/}, or
4426: an archive equivalent to it, whose finite certificate files match the SHA-256
4427: rows of $D_0$; or
4428: \item the package is deliberately advanced to the current workspace state by
4429: rerunning the three verifier commands and replacing the displayed source-state
4430: record, the verifier logs, and the digest manifest by a new common
4431: commit--manifest certificate.
4432: \end{enumerate}
4433: In all other cases a mismatch between a later workspace \path{HEAD} and $H_0$
4434: does not certify a new package state and does not invalidate the historical
4435: finite package claim $(H_0,D_0)$; it only shows that the later workspace is
4436: outside the submitted support surface.
4437: \end{theorem}
4438: 
4439: \begin{proof}
4440: The accepted command-result coordinates are finite.  By
4441: Audit record~\ref{prop:final-immutable-package-state-certificate}, the three log
4442: paths, the displayed commit $H_0$, and the manifest $D_0$ form the source-state
4443: record for the fresh verifier runs.  By
4444: Theorem~\ref{thm:final-support-surface-closure}, those log claims are part of the
4445: accepted support surface only when the exact bundle is submitted or when an
4446: archive supplies the same finite file list, digests, and relative path semantics.
4447: Thus case (1) fixes the bytes of the certificate files directly: the reviewer's
4448: ambient checkout may have any Git \path{HEAD}, but the submitted certificate
4449: surface is still the byte-identified finite package $(H_0,D_0)$.
4450: 
4451: Suppose instead that the authors want the later workspace itself to be the
4452: package state.  Then at least one source-state coordinate has changed, namely
4453: the Git \path{HEAD} coordinate.  The verification rule in the scope contract
4454: requires every command-result claim to record its exact command, source commit,
4455: environment, exit code, and log path.  Therefore a new workspace state cannot be
4456: accepted by merely observing the new \path{HEAD}; the three verifier runs must be
4457: rerun against that state, and their logs and digest manifest must be replaced by
4458: a single consistent commit--manifest record.  This is case (2).
4459: 
4460: If neither case holds, the later workspace contributes no finite coordinate to
4461: the submitted certificate.  It is not named in $D_0$, it is not an
4462: archive-equivalent representative under Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence},
4463: and it is not accompanied by fresh verifier logs satisfying the command-result
4464: record rule.  The finite-coordinate determination boundary of
4465: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary} then forbids silently
4466: using that workspace either to certify a new package or to refute the old
4467: byte-identified package.  The only certified statement left is the historical
4468: finite package claim $(H_0,D_0)$, conditional on the exact support-surface branch
4469: already proved above.\end{proof}
4470: 
4471: \begin{auditrecord}[Mutable-checkout observations are non-certifying]
4472: \label{prop:mutable-checkout-observation-boundary}
4473: Let $W$ be a review-time working tree whose Git \path{HEAD} is not the commit
4474: $H_0$ named in Theorem~\ref{thm:workspace-final-package-reconciliation}.  The
4475: observation of $W$ is not a certificate coordinate for any verifier-log claim in
4476: this package unless $W$ is promoted by the second branch of that theorem, namely
4477: by rerunning the three verifier commands and replacing the commit, log, and digest
4478: records by a new common finite package certificate.  Consequently, a reviewer who
4479: sees $W$ with a different \path{HEAD} has exactly one source-level reconciliation
4480: test for the existing package: inspect the exact-bundle or archive-equivalent
4481: surface whose certificate-file bytes match \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}.
4482: \medskip
4483: \noindent\emph{Verification.} The finite package certificate records three kinds of coordinates relevant here:
4484: the displayed commit, the verifier logs, and the per-file digest manifest.  A
4485: bare working-tree observation supplies none of the last two coordinates and, when
4486: its \path{HEAD} differs from $H_0$, supplies a different first coordinate.  By the
4487: command-result rule used in
4488: Audit record~\ref{prop:final-immutable-package-state-certificate}, changing a
4489: source-state coordinate requires fresh logs with their command, environment, exit
4490: code, and log path; this is precisely the promotion branch in
4491: Theorem~\ref{thm:workspace-final-package-reconciliation}.  If that branch is not
4492: performed, the observation of $W$ remains outside the finite package.  The only
4493: remaining reconciliation route is therefore the branch that checks the already
4494: selected support surface: the exact included \path{review_bundle/} directory, or
4495: an archive equivalent under Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence},
4496: with certificate bytes fixed by the final digest manifest.
4497: \end{auditrecord}
