4499: \begin{theorem}[Support-surface normal form for bundle-backed claims]
4500: \label{thm:support-surface-normal-form}
4501: For the current presentation package, every accepted use of a bundle-backed
4502: certificate coordinate is in exactly one of the following normal forms.
4503: \begin{enumerate}
4504: \item \emph{Exact inclusion}: an external upload or submission receipt records
4505: that the submitted support surface contains the exact \path{review_bundle/}
4506: directory whose certificate-file bytes match
4507: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md}.
4508: \item \emph{Archive-equivalent inclusion}: a replacement archive satisfies every
4509: row of Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}, including manifest
4510: identity, bundle-version identity, finite file-list identity, SHA-256 content
4511: identity, and relative path semantics.
4512: \item \emph{Promoted rerun}: the package is advanced to a new source state by
4513: rerunning the verifier commands and replacing the displayed source-state record,
4514: verifier logs, and digest manifest by one common finite commit--manifest
4515: certificate.
4516: \end{enumerate}
4517: If none of these three normal forms is present, the attempted bundle-backed
4518: reading has a finite obstruction subrecord: either the external exact-inclusion
4519: receipt is absent, the archive-equivalence table has a failed row, or the rerun
4520: branch lacks the command, source-state, environment, exit-code, log-path, and
4521: digest coordinates required by the command-boundary rule.  Thus the late
4522: support-surface chain is a finite audit-interface classification for this
4523: package, not a theorem about general archive infrastructure, venue upload, or
4524: semantic correctness of the bundled artifacts.
4525: \end{theorem}
4526: 
4527: \begin{proof}
4528: The candidate support surface for a bundle-backed coordinate can differ from the
4529: source-level package in only three record-visible ways.  First, it can supply an
4530: external receipt for the same directory selected by
4531: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention}.
4532: Theorem~\ref{thm:exact-inclusion-support-surface-realization} and
4533: Theorem~\ref{thm:final-support-surface-closure} prove that this exact directory,
4534: with the final digest manifest, is the local byte surface that must be supplied;
4535: the additional receipt is what turns that local selection into submitted support.
4536: This is normal form~(1).
4537: 
4538: Second, the candidate can replace the directory by an archive.  The manuscript
4539: does not accept arbitrary archive availability as a certificate coordinate:
4540: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} gives the finite
4541: hash-and-manifest test, and every failed row of
4542: Table~\ref{tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} is a finite bad subrecord.  If
4543: all rows pass, the replacement denotes the same certificate bytes under the same
4544: relative paths and is normal form~(2); if any row fails, the archive cannot carry
4545: the bundle-backed claim.
4546: 
4547: Third, the candidate can point to a later or different workspace state.
4548: Theorem~\ref{thm:workspace-final-package-reconciliation} proves that such a state
4549: is not the old finite package unless it is deliberately promoted by fresh verifier
4550: runs and by a replacement commit--manifest certificate.
4551: Audit record~\ref{prop:mutable-checkout-observation-boundary} then shows that a
4552: bare mutable-checkout observation is non-certifying.  Therefore a different
4553: workspace is accepted only in normal form~(3), and otherwise has the finite
4554: command-boundary obstruction stated in the theorem.
4555: 
4556: The three cases are mutually exclusive as record modes for a fixed submitted
4557: claim: the first uses the selected directory, the second uses a byte-identical
4558: archive representative, and the third replaces the package state and digest
4559: record by a new common certificate.  If a proposed support reading is in none of
4560: the modes, it contributes no coordinate read by the verifier.  By
4561: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary} and the obstruction
4562: skeleton of Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-certificate-obstruction-skeleton}, the missing
4563: coordinate is an inclusion-minimal finite bad subrecord rather than a semantic
4564: fact about the underlying artifacts.\end{proof}
4565: 
4566: \begin{theorem}[Upload instantiation boundary]
4567: \label{thm:upload-or-archive-instantiation-boundary}
4568: Before the bundle-backed claims of this supplement are treated as part of a
4569: completed venue submission, the external submission record must instantiate the
4570: support-surface branch selected by
4571: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention} and
4572: Theorems~\ref{thm:final-support-surface-closure} and
4573: \ref{thm:support-surface-normal-form}: it must record that
4574: \path{review_bundle/} was uploaded exactly with digest manifest $D_0$ and with
4575: the root \path{theorem_inventory.json} coordinate named by the manifest and
4576: ledger.  The TeX source and the local digest manifest select that exact-inclusion
4577: branch but do not constitute a venue upload receipt.  In the present source
4578: package no such external receipt is recorded; consequently all bundle-backed
4579: claims are proved only as conditional source-level support claims until the
4580: missing external exact-inclusion record is supplied.
4581: \end{theorem}
4582: 
4583: \begin{proof}
4584: Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention} and
4585: Theorem~\ref{thm:final-support-surface-closure} prove that the bundle-backed
4586: claims for this package are admissible in the exact-directory branch only.
4587: Audit record~\ref{prop:exact-review-bundle-upload-witness} and
4588: Audit record~\ref{prop:final-immutable-package-state-certificate} give the same
4589: selection and explicitly say that no archive locator is claimed.  Those source
4590: records determine what must be submitted, but they are produced before the
4591: venue's upload action and contain no venue receipt, DOI, institutional
4592: identifier, or external archive locator.  Hence a completed submission needs one
4593: additional external instantiation record: the venue or packager must record the
4594: exact supplemental directory upload with the final digest manifest.  Without that
4595: record, the statements proved above remain conditional source-level support
4596: claims rather than a proof that the upload action has occurred.  Therefore
4597: treating the bundle-backed claims as externally instantiated would add a
4598: coordinate not present in the finite support surface, contradicting the finite
4599: coordinate determination boundary of
4600: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary}.\end{proof}
4601: 
4602: \begin{corollary}[Upload-or-archive instantiation record]
4603: \label{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record}
4604: The bundle-backed support claims of the current package may be used only under
4605: the external-record condition of
4606: Theorem~\ref{thm:upload-or-archive-instantiation-boundary}.  In particular,
4607: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} is a local byte-level packaging
4608: manifest and not, by itself, an upload receipt or an archive locator; no archive
4609: replacement branch is selected for this source package.
4610: \end{corollary}
4611: 
4612: \begin{proof}
4613: This is the record-level specialization of
4614: Theorem~\ref{thm:upload-or-archive-instantiation-boundary} to the current digest
4615: manifest.\end{proof}
4616: 
4617: \begin{corollary}[Current no-receipt support-surface non-escalation]
4618: \label{cor:current-no-receipt-support-surface-non-escalation}
4619: In the current source package the records
4620: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md},
4621: \path{review_bundle/REVIEW_BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json},
4622: \path{review_bundle/current_package_pass_records.json}, and
4623: \path{theorem_inventory.json} do not contain a venue upload receipt, public DOI,
4624: institutional archive identifier, or archive-equivalent locator for
4625: \path{review_bundle/}.  Hence every claim whose evidence surface is a
4626: bundle-local path is accepted only as a conditional exact-supplemental-inclusion
4627: claim.  Such a claim becomes an externally instantiated submitted-support claim
4628: only after one of the two finite records below is added to the submitted support
4629: surface:
4630: \begin{enumerate}
4631: \item an upload receipt naming the exact \path{review_bundle/} directory and the
4632: final digest manifest; or
4633: \item an archive-equivalent locator satisfying the file-list, digest, manifest,
4634: and path-semantics tests of
4635: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}.
4636: \end{enumerate}
4637: Until then, the theorem inventory, verifier logs, case snapshots, source
4638: snapshot, and primary-claim inventory remain local/path-verified review-bundle
4639: coordinates rather than unconditional public or venue-submitted coordinates.
4640: \end{corollary}
4641: 
4642: \begin{proof}
4643: The four named files are the only finite records in the present source package
4644: that select the support branch for \path{review_bundle/}: the digest manifest
4645: gives the byte-level package identity, the review-bundle manifest gives the
4646: submission strategy, the pass-record ledger exposes the accepted finite gates,
4647: and \path{theorem_inventory.json} is the manual theorem-ledger coordinate.  Their
4648: recorded branch is exact supplemental inclusion and their archive fields state
4649: that no archive replacement or locator is claimed.  Therefore they determine the
4650: bytes and paths that must be supplied, but they do not determine that a venue
4651: upload, DOI minting event, institutional archiving event, or archive-equivalent
4652: publication event has occurred.
4653: 
4654: By Theorem~\ref{thm:upload-or-archive-instantiation-boundary}, an externally
4655: instantiated bundle-backed claim needs exactly the missing external coordinate:
4656: either an upload record for the exact directory and final digest manifest, or a
4657: replacement archive record passing
4658: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}.  By
4659: Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record}, the digest manifest
4660: alone is not such a coordinate.  If neither finite record is present, promoting a
4661: bundle-local path to an unconditional submitted-support coordinate would add an
4662: evidence coordinate not contained in the support surface, contrary to
4663: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary}.  The stated
4664: conditional boundary follows for every bundle-backed surface named in the
4665: corollary.
4666: \end{proof}
