4668: 
4669: \begin{proposition}[Primary architectural fallback without external support]
4670: \label{prop:primary-architectural-fallback-without-external-support}
4671: Assume the current source package is used without an upload receipt for the exact
4672: \path{review_bundle/} directory and without an archive-equivalent replacement
4673: satisfying Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence}.  Then the
4674: primary presentation article may assert only the source-level architecture and
4675: path-verified local-package claims whose evidence surfaces are visible outside the
4676: missing bundle.  In particular, the theorem-ledger claim of
4677: Theorem~\ref{thm:theorem-obligation-ledger-boundary}, the case-snapshot claims,
4678: the verifier-log claims, and any claim whose certificate coordinate is
4679: \path{theorem_inventory.json} or a file under \path{review_bundle/} cannot be
4680: read as externally submitted evidence.  If either accepted external instantiation
4681: record is later supplied, the same claims re-enter exactly at the finite evidence
4682: level stated in their certificate rows and not at any stronger semantic or venue
4683: acceptance level.
4684: \end{proposition}
4685: 
4686: \begin{proof}
4687: Corollary~\ref{cor:current-no-receipt-support-surface-non-escalation} identifies
4688: the only two records that can externally instantiate a bundle-backed support
4689: claim: an exact upload receipt for \path{review_bundle/} with the final digest
4690: manifest, or an archive-equivalent locator passing the finite file-list, digest,
4691: manifest, and path-semantics tests.  Under the present hypothesis neither record
4692: is available.  Hence every bundle-local path is absent from the externally
4693: submitted finite support surface.
4694: 
4695: The affected claims are precisely those whose certificate coordinate names such a
4696: path.  Table~\ref{tab:submitted-theorem-obligation-ledger} places the manual
4697: theorem inventory at \path{theorem_inventory.json} and exposes it through
4698: \path{review_bundle/current_package_pass_records.json}; the case-snapshot and
4699: verifier-log statements similarly name files under \path{review_bundle/}.  By
4700: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary}, a claim cannot acquire
4701: an evidence coordinate that is absent from the finite support surface.  Therefore
4702: those claims cannot be read as externally submitted evidence while both accepted
4703: instantiation records are missing.
4704: 
4705: Removing that external reading does not remove the primary article's independent
4706: architectural assertion.  The primary text describes the compiler's typed record
4707: interface and cites the pinned public source surface; those claims do not require
4708: the missing bundle-local coordinate.  If a valid exact-upload or
4709: archive-equivalent record is later supplied, Theorem~\ref{thm:support-surface-normal-form}
4710: and Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-or-archive-instantiation-record} put the
4711: bundle-backed claims back into the finite support surface.  The reinstatement is
4712: only at the recorded evidence levels, because the same corollaries and
4713: Theorem~\ref{thm:upload-or-archive-instantiation-boundary} exclude stronger
4714: readings such as semantic proof checking, fresh dynamic validation, venue
4715: compliance, or acceptance.\end{proof}
