4874: \begin{theorem}[Seven-row submitted theorem-obligation ledger integration]
4875: \label{thm:theorem-obligation-ledger-boundary}
4876: Let $P^{+}_{7}$ be the seven-row support state obtained from $P^{+}_{6}$
4877: by the conservative finite-record extension of
4878: Theorem~\ref{thm:nested-package-states}, namely by adding exactly the manual
4879: submitted theorem-ledger coordinate \path{a7}.  In
4880: $P^{+}_{7}$, the theorem-obligation ledger is no longer a detached review-only
4881: artifact: the submitted finite support surface contains
4882: \path{theorem_inventory.json} through the manifest field \path{theorem_inventory}
4883: and through acceptance-ledger entry \path{a7}.  The earlier six-row state
4884: $P^{+}_{6}$ of Theorems~\ref{thm:nested-package-states}
4885: and~\ref{thm:current-package-certificate-exactness} remains
4886: the row-frozen certificate state for \path{a1}--\path{a6}; the present theorem
4887: adds exactly the manual theorem-ledger coordinate \path{a7}.  Consequently the
4888: package may make
4889: the following bounded theorem-ledger claim: every theorem-obligation assertion
4890: made by the submission is supported only through the finite coordinates in
4891: Table~\ref{tab:submitted-theorem-obligation-ledger}, namely the integrated
4892: theorem inventory, the primary-claim inventory, the certificate ledger, and the
4893: manifest exposure records.  By
4894: Proposition~\ref{prop:manual-theorem-inventory-boundary}, this is a manual
4895: Stage-A obligation ledger claim, not a deterministic theorem-environment
4896: extraction or completeness claim.  The claim does not assert that
4897: \path{theorem_inventory.json} proves the mathematical semantics of each theorem,
4898: does not replace the proofs printed in this source, and does not certify a Lean
4899: rebuild, publication-daemon run, Rule110 artifact rerun, extractor run, or
4900: external upload.
4901: \end{theorem}
4902: 
4903: \begin{proof}
4904: The support surface is finite and can be inspected coordinate by coordinate.
4905: The root manifest now contains the key \path{theorem_inventory} with value
4906: \path{theorem_inventory.json}.  The certificate schema includes the same key in
4907: its required manifest-file map.  Therefore a certificate-record verification of
4908: the enlarged package must check that the manifest exposes this root-level
4909: inventory path and that the file is present.  This removes the previous
4910: possibility of silently citing a root-level Stage-A artifact outside the support
4911: surface.
4912: 
4913: The acceptance ledger contains the additional entry \path{a7}.  Its accepted
4914: claim is exactly the bounded submitted theorem-obligation ledger claim; its
4915: claim kinds are \path{traceability} and \path{submission}.  Under the schema's
4916: gate dispatch, those kinds require the inventory, marker-existence, and
4917: submission-pack gates.  Entry \path{a7} supplies precisely those three pass
4918: records: the inventory gate points to \path{theorem_inventory.json}, the
4919: marker-existence gate points to
4920: Table~\ref{tab:submitted-theorem-obligation-ledger}, and the submission-pack
4921: gate points to \path{review_bundle/REVIEW_BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json}.  Thus the
4922: ledger supplies a finite route from the theorem-inventory file to the submitted
4923: certificate records rather than a prose-only reference.
4924: 
4925: It remains to identify the boundary.  The schema-level verifier checks finite
4926: record shape, required manifest paths, gate coverage, evidence pointers, and
4927: evidence levels.  None of those checks is a semantic proof of the theorem-like
4928: environments in this source, and none reruns Lean, the publication daemon, the
4929: Rule110/GroundCompiler artifacts, or an independent theorem-environment
4930: extractor.  Proposition~\ref{prop:manual-theorem-inventory-boundary} supplies the
4931: missing classification: the inventory is an accepted manual Stage-A ledger and
4932: not an executable completeness certificate.  The theorem-ledger claim is
4933: therefore admissible only at the path-verified evidence level stated in
4934: \path{a7}.  The mathematical content of the article remains carried by the
4935: printed definitions, propositions, lemmas, theorems, and proofs, and external
4936: records carry only the finite evidence claims that cite them.  The integrated
4937: inventory gives the submitted finite obligation surface against which those
4938: theorem-like claims are enumerated; it indexes the obligations and does not prove
4939: them.  This is exactly the bounded claim stated in the theorem.
4940: \end{proof}
